```

# Absolute value

## Definition of absolute value

**Definition:** for any $x \in \mathbb{R}$ we set
$$
|x| =
\begin{cases}
\phantom{-}x & \text{if } x \geq 0 \\[5mm]
-x & \text{if } x < 0
\end{cases}
$$

**Examples:** $|{-3.14}| = 3.14$, $\;|0| = 0$, $\;|2| = 2$.

```coq
(* Note that in Rocq, the proof assistant Waterproof is built on,
   |x| is called Rabs x, defined in Stdlib.Reals.Rbasic_fun. *)
```

## Absolute value and maximum

**Lemma:** $|x| = \max\{x, -x\}$

**Proof:**
- If $x \geq 0$: $-x \leq 0 \leq x$, so $\max\lbrace -x,x \rbrace = x = |x|$.
- If $x < 0$: $-x > 0 > x$, so $\max\lbrace -x,x \rbrace = -x = |x|$.

```coq
Lemma abs_eq_max (x : ℝ) : Rabs x = Rmax x (- x).
Proof.
  Either x ≥ 0 or x < 0.
  - Case x ≥ 0.
    It holds that Rabs x = x as (H1).
    It holds that Rmax x (- x) = x as (H2).
    We conclude that Rabs x = Rmax x (- x).
  - Case x < 0.
    It holds that Rabs x = - x as (H1).
    It holds that Rmax x (- x) = - x as (H2).
    We conclude that Rabs x = Rmax x (- x).
Qed.
```

## Product rule

**Lemma:** $|xy| = |x|\\,|y|$

**Proof:** case analysis on the signs of $x$ and $y$.

```coq
Lemma abs_mult (x y : ℝ) : Rabs (x * y) = Rabs x * Rabs y.
Proof.
  By Rabs_mult we conclude that Rabs (x * y) = Rabs x * Rabs y.
Qed.
```

## Quotient rule

**Lemma:** $\displaystyle\left|\frac{x}{y}\right| = \frac{|x|}{|y|}$ for $y\neq 0$.

**Proof:** $x/y = x \cdot (1/y)$, $|1/y| = 1/|y|$, and use the product rule.

```coq
Lemma abs_div (x y : ℝ) (Hy : y ≠ 0) : Rabs (x / y) = Rabs x / Rabs y.
Proof.
  By Rabs_inv it holds that Rabs (/ y) = / Rabs y.
  We conclude that Rabs (x / y) = Rabs x / Rabs y.
Qed.
```

## Triangle inequality

**Lemma (Triangle inequality):**
$$
|x + y| \leq |x| + |y|
$$

**Proof:**
$$\begin{aligned}
x+y & \leq |x| + y \leq |x| + |y| \\[3mm]
{-x}-y & \leq |x| - y \leq |x| + |y| \\[3mm]
|x+y| & = \max\{x+y, -x-y\} \leq |x| + |y|
\end{aligned}$$

```coq
Lemma triangle_inequality (x y : ℝ) : Rabs (x + y) ≤ Rabs x + Rabs y.
Proof.
  (* Exercise, prove it without calling the corresponding statement in the library *)
  By Rabs_triang we conclude that Rabs (x + y) ≤ Rabs x + Rabs y.
Qed.
```

## Reverse triangle inequality

**Lemma (Reverse triangle inequality):**
$$
\big||x| - |y|\big| \leq |x - y|
$$

**Proof:**
$$\begin{aligned}
|x| = |x-y+y| & \leq |x-y| + |y| \implies |x| - |y| \leq |x-y| \\[3mm]
|y| - |x| & \leq |y-x| = |x-y| \quad\text{(swap $x$ and $y$)} \\[3mm]
\big||x| - |y|\big| & = \max\{|x|-|y|,\,|y|-|x|\} \leq |x-y|
\end{aligned}$$

```coq
Lemma reverse_triangle_inequality (x y : ℝ) : Rabs (Rabs x - Rabs y) ≤ Rabs (x - y).
Proof.
  (* Exercise, prove it without calling the corresponding statement in the library *)
  By Rabs_triang_inv2 we conclude that Rabs (Rabs x - Rabs y) ≤ Rabs (x - y).
Qed.
```
